{"UsernameForm.authenticate() calls isConditionalPasskeysEnabled() with no arguments, but the only available method requires a UserModel parameter, causing a compile-time error that will block the build": 0.4987983703613281, "Conditional passkeys are only enabled when user != null, which prevents setting up conditional UI on initial login pages where context.getUser() is typically null, breaking discoverable-key passkey login that relies on the ID-less path": 0.41521164774894714, "Some new UI tests assert absence of elements by catching Exception instead of NoSuchElementException, which can incorrectly treat unrelated WebDriver failures as 'element absent' and make tests pass when the page is actually broken/flaky": 0.7606560587882996}